INT. DRAGON DENTIST'S CAVERN - DAY

A great cavern hung with brass lamps. A chair carved from a single glacial boulder. Around it, racks of tongs and chisels the size of oars. A bubbling cauldron of mouthwash.

DR. HOLLYHOCK THISTLEWICK, 200 and spry, tiny, a mirror-headed lamp strapped to her brow, stands on a ladder, peering into a mouth the size of a barn door. A DRAGON lies in the chair, jaws wide, one golden eye rolling.

PIP, a pixie nurse no bigger than a thimble, buzzes at the dentist's ear with a tray of silver picks. GRUB, a goblin receptionist, leans in the doorway chewing a pencil. SIR ALARIC FENWICK-DALE, a very old knight, sits in the waiting alcove with his helmet in his lap.

HOLLYHOCK
Wider, please.

DRAGON
(muffled)
Wider than this?

HOLLYHOCK
I'm afraid so.

DRAGON
(muffled)
You said that last time.

HOLLYHOCK
And the time before. Wider.

He strains. The cavern shudders. A stalactite falls and bounces off Sir Alaric's helmet.

SIR ALARIC
Ow.

GRUB
Sorry, Sir Alaric. Occupational hazard.

HOLLYHOCK
Pip, the number seven pick.

PIP
Coming, Doctor.

Hollyhock probes. The dragon's tail thumps once. Dust rains from the ceiling.

HOLLYHOCK (CONT'D)
Your gum is inflamed, Veskarath.

VESKARATH
(muffled)
It's been like that for three centuries.

HOLLYHOCK
It's gingivitis.

VESKARATH
It's a lifestyle.

HOLLYHOCK
You've eaten a lot of knights.

VESKARATH
(muffled, a little ashamed)
Only the crunchy ones.

Sir Alaric clears his throat. Rises from the alcove, helmet under one arm.

SIR ALARIC
I was told this would be a quick consultation.

HOLLYHOCK
It always is, Sir Alaric.

SIR ALARIC
It's been four hours.

GRUB
Time moves differently in a cave.

VESKARATH
(muffled)
Is that supposed to be a joke?

GRUB
It's a policy.

Hollyhock sighs. Climbs down the ladder, pats the dragon's lip, and picks up a small mirror.

HOLLYHOCK
Rinse and spit. Then floss.

VESKARATH
Floss what?

HOLLYHOCK
(to Sir Alaric, deadpan)
You'll do.
